// CACHE: GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits | owner=CodeEditorLand | repo=Land | per_page=5 | page=81 → GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/commits.RESPONSE.map(Author,Date,File,Message,SHA)
{
	"Set": [
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T01:47:53Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				100,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Project): Coordinate submodule updates for extension host reliability\n\nFour submodule updates improve extension activation and webview compatibility:\n- **Mountain**: Treat view registry commands (<viewId>.focus, .resetViewLocation, .removeView) as silent no-ops to eliminate GitLens error spam. Also preserve VSIX executable bits (0o755) during extraction so extensions with native binaries (codex, language servers) can spawn correctly.\n- **Output**: Add StripWebviewIframeSandbox transform plugin to remove sandbox attribute from VS Code's webview iframe. WKWebView blocks custom protocol loads (vscode-webview://, land://) from sandboxed iframes, breaking extension webview panels.\n- **Echo**: Submodule sync for task scheduler alignment.\n- **Cocoon**: Submodule sync for extension host alignment.\n\nImpact: Extensions with native binaries now activate correctly, extension webview panels load in Tauri, and spurious error logs are eliminated.",
			"SHA": "ae825d2c75e042f9b65ae397c3ea7e0160b43e7b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T01:29:16Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				100,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Handle ILocalExtension envelope shape in extension scanner\n\nMountain's scanSystem/UserExtensions now returns ILocalExtension-wrapped objects with nested manifest, identifier.id, and location fields, rather than the flat structure the scanner previously expected. This caused all extensions to appear as 'unknown' with empty names/publishers in the sidebar.\n\nThe fix reads the nested ext.manifest first, falls back to flat ext for backward compatibility. Also maps: location (new) / extensionLocation (old), identifier.id (new) / identifier.value (old), and properly propagates targetPlatform, isValid, and validationMessages instead of hardcoded defaults.\n\nThis ensures the @builtin/@installed extension split works correctly in the Extensions sidebar.",
			"SHA": "cf9e5e4553a92c5bb2acc4525ca38669931e5bd5"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T01:21:10Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				100,
				1
			],
			"Message": "build(Project): Coordinate extension scanning and file URI handling fixes\n\nThree related fixes improve extension host integration:\n- **Mountain:** Add `StripFileUriScheme()` helper to strip `file://` or `file:///` prefixes from URIs before creating PathBuf. Applies to all 8 FileSystem operations (ReadFile, WriteFile, ReadDirectory, StatFile, CreateDirectory, Delete, Rename, Copy). This fixes redhat.java extension activation failure with \"Resource not found: file:///...\" errors.\n- **Output:** Separate system and user extension scanning in ExtensionScannerIPC. Now calls `extensions:scanSystemExtensions` for ForceBuiltin=true and `extensions:scanUserExtensions` for ForceBuiltin=false. Previously all extensions were hardcoded as builtin, causing user VSIXes to appear under @builtin in the sidebar. Also implements the stubbed `scanUserExtensions()` method.\n- **Cocoon:** Minor submodule sync.\n\nImpact: User-installed extensions now appear under \"Installed\" (not \"Built-in\") and file operations correctly resolve paths from gRPC FileSystem calls.",
			"SHA": "a672e28212a9effc120c8f7d8074f8043d6cc3a3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T00:40:30Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				100,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Wind): Align FileSystemProviderError names with VS Code's token format\n\nWind's FileSystemErrorCode uses key-like values ('FileNotFound', 'FileExists'), but VS Code's toFileSystemProviderErrorCode extracts the token from error.name and switches on 'EntryNotFound', 'EntryExists', etc. Add a mapping function VsCodeErrorCodeToken to translate between the two formats. Also set this.name to the '<code> (FileSystemError)' pattern that VS Code's markAsFileSystemProviderError() expects. Remove individual name assignments from subclasses since the base class now handles naming.\n\nWithout this fix, mkdirp and validateWriteFile treat missing-file/dir errors as unknown and rethrow, surfacing as unhandled rejections like 'Unable to write file .../tasks.log (Error: Failed to stat file ...)'.\n\nThis is a coordinated update with Cocoon (submodule sync).",
			"SHA": "6682d648fc1c3b599493c5a6d71ef0f66c4d6d40"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-23T00:29:07Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				100,
				1
			],
			"Message": "build(Project): Coordinate extension compatibility and IPC channel fixes across 4 components\n\nSynchronize Cocoon, Mountain, Output, and Wind submodules with the following changes:\n- **Cocoon:** Add missing TextEditorCursorStyle (.Line, .Block, etc.) and UIKind (.Desktop, .Web) enums that extensions like vscodevim and gitlens depend on at activation. Also add stub terminal shell-integration event handlers to prevent crashes.\n- **Mountain:** Return correct Cocoon PID via GetCocoonPid() instead of Mountain's own PID. The renderer needs this to correlate extension-host debug adapters with the actual Node.js process. Also register walkthrough commands as no-ops for claude-code extension.\n- **Output:** Fix CatchOutputFolderRejection regex to match both `() => undefined` and minified `() => void 0`. Correct userDataSync channel names: `userDataSyncService` → `userDataSync`, `userDataSync` → `userDataSyncAccount` per VS Code source.\n- **Wind:** Sync userDataSync IPC channel names to match Output and VS Code registration.\n\nImpact: Extensions with cursor styling and UI detection now activate without crashes, debug adapters attach to the correct process, and user data sync IPC routes correctly.",
			"SHA": "d7fba66f9a270bf7c4e66bf085e305a432b49128"
		}
	],
	"TimeStamp": 1783259760985
}